Third-party material, not covered by the licences above:
- mckay_r45_24_line3521.g6 and mckay_r55_42some_line94.g6 are single lines copied unchanged from B. D. McKay's
  Ramsey graph lists (https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/data/ramsey.html, files r45_24.g6 and r55_42some.g6);
  H24.txt and H42.txt are their complements, and the two graphs contain these complements as induced subgraphs.
  We found no licence or terms of use stated on McKay's page. They are included as mathematical data, with their
  source named; please credit B. D. McKay and the authors named on his page when you use them.
- G384.txt (built by build_g384.py from the published rule of R. Mathon, JCTB 42 (1987), in the form of X. Xu and
  S. P. Radziszowski, EJC 16 (2009) #N1) is a mathematical construction from the literature; the two graphs contain
  it as an induced subgraph. It is identical to rows 0 to 383 of Byungkun Jang's r5-21/R5_21_444.txt
  (github.com/8rulerstar/ramsey-lower-bounds, graph files under CC BY 4.0, credit Byungkun Jang), where we first
  obtained it.
